  "donationEduQuotiteBody": "The disposable portion is the part of your wealth you can freely donate or bequeath without encroaching on the reserved portions. Since January 1, 2023, the children's reserved portion has been reduced from 3/4 to 1/2 of their legal share, and parents no longer have a reserved portion. This gives you more freedom to make donations.",
  "donationEduAvancementTitle": "Advancement of inheritance vs separate donation",
  "donationEduAvancementBody": "An advancement of inheritance is an advance on the beneficiary's share of the estate. It will be reported to the estate upon death. A separate donation (or preciput) is charged only to the disposable portion and is not reported. The choice between the two has a major impact on the balance between heirs.",
