  "concubinageInheritanceConditional": "Without a will, your partner inherits nothing: your estate goes to your legal heirs. With a will, what you can leave them depends on your descendants: if you have any, their statutory share is half of the estate, so the disposable portion is capped at the other half; if you have none, the parents' statutory share was abolished on 1 January 2023 and you may dispose of the whole estate (CC art. 470-471). What enters the estate is your share: property held in co-ownership counts only up to your own portion.",
  "concubinageInheritanceRateLimit": "No rate is shown here, deliberately: the burden ranges from zero in some cantons to nearly half of the share received in the heaviest ones, with progressive scales, allowances and sometimes a communal tax. Four things determine it: your canton and municipality, the share actually received, the family link, and how long you have lived together.",
